From 8176d859031eccc787a9e84373cb75000cb6889b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:57:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dynarmic A64: loops keep their busiest guest registers in
 host registers; the PS4 extras on with Auto again

- loop_register_pins: a block whose terminal links back to its own start keeps up to three of the
  guest registers it uses (those carried round the loop first) in rbx, rbp and r12 from its start
  to every exit: GetX/GetW/GetSP read them with moves, SetX/SetW/SetSP write them with moves, the
  written ones are stored back at each exit (side exits included), and the way back jumps past
  the loads after its halt check. Not with anything that reads the guest registers from the JIT
  state, leaves without its terminal (CheckHalt, supervisor calls, exceptions, halts on memory
  access) or needs rbx (exclusives, ordered 128-bit accesses). Checked: 60,000 random loop bodies
  (tools/jit-difftest loops) against no optimisation; a build that skips the stores fails 183 of 300.
- follow_known_returns (off): a RET whose X30 the block set to a followed BL's return address goes
  on in the block, the BL's return stack entry dropped.
- arm_dynarmic_64/32: the PS4 translator extras (64-bit 04.22-04.30, 32-bit 04.04-04.22) on with
  CPU Auto again (04.35/04.38-04.72 only with Unsafe, a diagnostic switch for problems that turned
  out to be elsewhere), off with Accurate, Paranoid and Debugging; loop pins likewise.
